Investigating ML/AI Models

This document provides a comprehensive comparative analysis of Machine Learning, Deep Learning, and Reinforcement Learning models investigated for Low-Rate Distributed Denial of Service (LDDoS) detection and mitigation.

---

## 1. supervised Models

| Model | Concept | Pros | Cons | How It Helps the Detection Idea |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **MLP** | Fully connected dense layers; every node connects to every node in the next layer. | Simple, pre-engineered static feature classification (Baseline). | Completely blind to both spatial structure and temporal sequences. | **Baseline Comparison:** Used only as a basic reference point to prove how much better our hybrid model performs. |
| **CNN (Convolutional)** | Uses local filters (kernels) to extract spatial feature maps. | Capturing local byte layouts and signature payloads within single packets. | Blind to long-term sequential dependencies across time. | **Spatial Extraction:** Extracts spatial features and packet layouts from the flow. |
| **RNN / LSTM** | Passes memory step-by-step to understand the sequence of events. | Tracking multi-stage attacks and slow scanning behaviors over time. | Slow training on GPUs (due to sequential nature); vanilla RNN suffers from vanishing gradients. | **Temporal Analysis:** Analyzes the temporal behavior of flows over time and detects complex attacks. |
| **Transformers** | Uses Self-Attention to map relationships between all input tokens simultaneously. | Deeply analyzing complex global relationships across massive network flows. | Heavy memory bottleneck and extreme GPU resource demands. | **Global Context:** Connects the dots between separate, long-range network events that happen far apart in time. |
| **Mamba (SSM)** | Uses Selective State Space Models (SSM) to compress context into a smart, fixed-size state. | High-speed, real-time enterprise traffic monitoring and long-duration log analysis. | Relatively new paradigm; fewer pre-trained models and community implementations compared to Transformers. | **Ultra-Fast Scanning:** Runs linear-time scanning over massive streams of enterprise traffic data without delay. |
| **LNNs (Liquid Networks)** | Uses continuous-time differential equations that adapt weight parameters dynamically at runtime. | Resource-constrained IoT/Embedded security where network conditions change unpredictably. | Highly complex and mathematically difficult to train initially on standard deep learning frameworks. | **Concept Drift Adaptation:** Adjusts parameters at runtime to capture unpredictable, evolving mutation attacks. |

